Problem:
A garbage collection company uses two types of vehicles, truck A and truck B. Truck A requires 3 workers while truck B requires 4 workers. Truck A can collect 40 units of garbage and truck B can collect 50 units of garbage. The garbage collection company has employed 150 workers. The company must use more truck A models than truck B models. Additionally, there must be at least 5 truck A’s and 8 truck B’s. How many of each type of vehicles should the company use to maximize the total amount of garbage that can be collected?

